  "label": "woman with visible injuries",
  "description": "The central visual entity, a woman with physical injuries, is presented as the symbolic representation of the suffering that motivates the demand for equal rights. This framing targets audiences who may be sympathetic to the plight of women experiencing violence, or who are familiar with narratives that link personal trauma to social justice movements. The image leverages emotional appeal to evoke empathy and validate the call for equal rights, suggesting the target audience is likely to be individuals who resonate with or support gender equality causes, but also potentially those who are susceptible to pity narratives or misogynous framing that reduces systemic issues to individual victimhood.",
